IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`
IMPORT `oapa-table`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- TESTS for oapa-table.l4.
--
-- The three tables below were written out by hand from the text of each section: the
-- word the section uses for its offence ("guilty of felony", "guilty of a misdemeanor",
-- "guilty of an offence", or none), the words that say how it is tried (sections 16 and
-- 47 "on indictment", sections 39, 40 and 42 "before two justices"), and the penalty
-- clause.  The table module calls each section's own rule; these assertions check that
-- it picked the right one for all 32 offences.

§ `Tests: the table of offences`

§§ `What the text calls each offence`

#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 4: soliciting or proposing a murder` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 5: manslaughter (the penalty only)` EQUALS `no classification stated`
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 16: threats to kill` EQUALS `an offence, with no further classification`
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 17: impeding a person trying to save their life from shipwreck` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 18: wounding or causing grievous bodily harm, with intent` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 20: wounding or inflicting grievous bodily harm` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 21: attempting to choke or render insensible, to commit an indictable offence` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 22: administering a stupefying drug, to commit an indictable offence` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 23: administering poison so as to endanger life or inflict grievous bodily harm` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 24: administering poison with intent to injure, aggrieve or annoy` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 26: neglecting or harming an apprentice or servant` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 27: abandoning or exposing a child under two years` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 28: causing bodily injury by an explosion` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 29: causing an explosion, or sending or applying a dangerous thing, with intent` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 30: placing an explosive near a building, ship or vessel, with intent` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 31: setting a spring gun or man trap` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 32: placing an obstruction on a railway, with intent to endanger` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 33: casting a thing at a railway carriage, with intent` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 34: endangering railway passengers` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 35: bodily harm by furious driving or wilful misconduct` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 36: obstructing or assaulting a clergyman or other minister` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 37: assaulting a person preserving a vessel or wreck` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 38: assault with intent to resist or prevent lawful apprehension` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 39: violence to obstruct the sale or conveyance of grain` EQUALS `no classification stated`
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 40: violence to hinder a seaman, keelman or caster` EQUALS `no classification stated`
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 42: common assault or battery` EQUALS `no classification stated`
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 47: assault occasioning actual bodily harm` EQUALS `no classification stated`
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 57: bigamy` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 58: administering drugs or using instruments to procure abortion` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 59: supplying drugs or instruments to procure abortion` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 60: concealing the birth of a child` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `the text calls the offence` `s 64: making or having gunpowder or a dangerous thing to commit a felony of this Act` EQUALS misdemeanor

